{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>תחת</b> The meaning is that the tents of Cushan fell, as though they were planted in places of iniquity so that they would not endure. It is also fitting that this is an allusion to the matter of Cushan-Rishathaim and the land of Midian regarding the matter of Gideon in the matter of the dream."], :book :habakkuk, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["<b>Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk</b>- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"] ["Ibn Ezra on Habakkuk -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/havakuk"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:56.832350675Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}